# /zigtrack, the admin family. The command.desc.* keys are what the engine's own help resolves a command or
# an argument's description from.
command.desc.family = Read and move players' tracks.
command.desc.add = Move a player's track, the way a reward would.
command.desc.show = Show a player's tracks, online or not.
command.desc.prestige = Start a player's climb on a track again.
command.desc.pick = Make a pick on a player's track: choose an offered option, or give a pick bought outright, past its level, wherever it is taught and without charging its price.
command.desc.undo = Undo a player's latest pick that can still be undone.
command.desc.respec = Clear every pick a player made on a track and give back the points. What a trainer taught stays.
command.desc.savebuild = Save the picks a player has in use on a track as one of their saved builds.
command.desc.swapbuild = Swap a player's picks on a track for one of their saved builds, paying the swap's price.
command.desc.builds = List a player's saved builds on a track.
command.desc.respend = Spend again, in order, the picks a prestige set aside on a track, as far as the points allow.
command.desc.starter = Spend what is left of a track's suggested build for a player, in order, as far as their points allow.
command.desc.lamp = Hand a player lamps: minutes of play they put into tracks of their choice, each at their level there.
command.desc.arg.price = A row of the XP price table: how many minutes each pick pays.
command.desc.arg.minutes = Minutes of play each pick pays, in place of the price row's.
command.desc.arg.price.level = Price each pick at this level for everyone, whatever their level on the track.
command.desc.arg.maxlevel = Price each pick at the player's level on the track, never above this one.
command.desc.arg.picks = How many different tracks the player picks, each paid in full.
command.desc.arg.tracks = The tracks it may go to, by id, split by commas. Leave it out for every track of the category.
command.desc.arg.category = With no tracks named, every track of this category. Leave it out for every track.
command.desc.arg.minlevel = The level a track must stand at for the player to pick it.
command.desc.arg.quantity = How many lamps, up to one stack.
command.desc.arg.points = Spend only the suggested build's first this many points. Leave it out for the whole build.
command.desc.arg.slot = Which saved build, by its number.
command.desc.arg.force = Swap even when no saved build holds the picks in use. Those picks are lost.
command.desc.arg.option = The option to choose, by its id.
command.desc.arg.pick = The pick, by its id.
command.desc.arg.level = The level of the choice to make. Leave it out for the lowest one waiting that offers the option.
command.desc.arg.player = The player, who has to be online. Defaults to you.
command.desc.arg.player.any = The player: a name for someone online, or a player id for someone who is not. Defaults to you.
command.desc.arg.track = The track, by its id.
command.desc.arg.amount = How much to add. A negative amount takes some away.
command.desc.arg.exact = Add the amount as it is, past every bonus and boost. The world's rules and the track's level cap still apply.
command.player.needed = Name a player with --player=<name>.
command.player.offline = That player is not in a world right now. Try again in a moment.
command.player.unknown = Could not find a player called '{0}'. Their player id works too.
command.track.needed = Name a track with --track=<id>.
command.track.unknown = No track called '{0}' is switched on here.
command.amount.needed = Name an amount with --amount=<n>, other than zero.
command.add.price.nothing = That price pays nothing on {0}: its curve has no Pace, or the price names no minutes.
command.lamp.needed = Name what each pick pays with --price=<id> or --minutes=<n>.
command.lamp.refused = No lamp could be handed to {0}.
command.lamp.done = Handed {0, number} {0, plural, one {lamp} other {lamps}} to {1}.
