# The World Rules screen on the owner menu (OwnerForms/Track_World_Rules.json), which edits track-world-rules.json one
# rule at a time.
form.rules.title = World Rules
form.rules.desc = How each world's rules change what tracks gain there and what their picks grant. Pick a rule to change it.
form.rules.note = Which worlds a rule covers, and every new rule, are written in the files: a pack's TrackWorldRules folder, mods/ziggfreedcommon/track-world-rules.json, or a world's own gameplay config. To switch every rule off at once, use the switch above the list of rules.
form.rules.on = This rule applies
form.rules.on.hint = Off keeps the rule but applies it nowhere, so its worlds follow the next rule that names them.
form.rules.heading.gain = Gains here
form.rules.gain.on = Gains land here
form.rules.gain.on.hint = Off stops every gain on every track in these worlds.
form.rules.multiplier = Multiplier
form.rules.multiplier.hint = What every gain is multiplied by here: 1 is unchanged, 2 doubles it, 0 stops it.
form.rules.disabled = Tracks that gain nothing
form.rules.disabled.hint = Track or category ids, split by commas. These gain nothing here, whatever the list below says.
form.rules.allowed = Only these tracks gain
form.rules.allowed.hint = Track or category ids, split by commas. When it names any, every track it leaves out gains nothing here. Left blank, the rule's own list applies.
form.rules.hits = Hits on players pay
form.rules.hits.hint = On lets a hit on another player pay here the way a hit on a creature does, for a PvP arena whose fights should train.
form.rules.heading.grants = What picks grant here
form.rules.grants.on = Grants stay on
form.rules.grants.on.hint = Off takes away everything the picks grant while a player is here. Leaving the world gives it back.
form.rules.ability = Abilities
form.rules.ability.hint = Off takes away the grants in the Ability family here, and switches abilities off here for a mod that reads this switch.
form.rules.combat = Combat Bonuses
form.rules.combat.hint = Off takes away the grants in the Combat family here.
form.rules.stat = Stat Bonuses
form.rules.stat.hint = Off takes away the stats the picks grant here. A stat in a family switched on above stays.
# The Level Curves screen on the owner menu (OwnerForms/Track_Curves.json), which edits track-curves.json one curve at
# a time. In form.curves.preview {0}, {2}, {4} and {6} are levels and {1}, {3}, {5} and {7} the value each one takes.
form.curves.title = Level Curves
form.curves.desc = How much each level takes on the curves tracks climb. Pick a curve to change it.
form.curves.heading = The formula
form.curves.note = Each level costs the sum of floor(l + Scale x 2^(l / 7)) over the levels below it, quartered, plus Base x level x (level - 1) / 2. Saving writes the whole formula into track-curves.json, which then wins over any other setting for this curve.
form.curves.base = Base
form.curves.base.hint = The steady part. Higher makes every level slower by the same share.
form.curves.scale = Scale
form.curves.scale.hint = The part that doubles about every seven levels. Higher makes the late levels much slower.
form.curves.preview = To reach level {0, number}: {1, number}. Level {2, number}: {3, number}. Level {4, number}: {5, number}. Level {6, number}: {7, number}.
# The Respec Prices screen on the owner menu (OwnerForms/Track_Respec.json), which edits tracks.json one track at a time.
form.respec.title = Respec Prices
form.respec.desc = What a player pays to reset a track's picks, at a trainer or on its tree. Pick a track to change it.
form.respec.note = A reset costs the track's respec price once for every share of the player's best level written here. What the price is paid in stays in tracks.json.
form.respec.per_level = Paid per level
form.respec.per_level.hint = How many times the price is paid for each level of the player's best level, rounded up. Half is once every two levels. Zero pays it once, whatever the level.
form.curves.heading.pace = Pace
form.curves.pace.note = How much an hour of steady play earns from each level on. A reward priced in minutes pays that many minutes of the band the player stands in.
form.curves.pace = Bands
form.curves.pace.hint = Each band is the level it starts at, an equals sign and the amount an hour from there, split by commas: 1=16000, 10=22000. A band you leave out keeps its usual amount. A band of 0 takes one out.
form.prices.title = XP Prices
form.prices.desc = How many minutes of play each kind of reward pays: quests, board jobs, dungeon clears, achievements. Pick one to change it.
form.prices.note = A reward names one of these. It pays that many minutes at the pace of the skill it goes to, worked out when the player earns it.
form.prices.minutes = Minutes
form.prices.minutes.hint = How many minutes of steady play it pays. 0 pays nothing.
form.prices.level = At level
form.prices.level.hint = Pay everyone the minutes of this level. For one-off content made for a level. 0 uses the player's own level.
form.prices.maxlevel = Up to level
form.prices.maxlevel.hint = When it uses the player's own level, never go above this one, so easy repeatable content stops paying more. 0 sets no limit.
form.keys.title = Diminishing Keys
form.keys.desc = What a source's diminishing returns count per: a spot, a kind of thing, a station or one creature. Pick one to change it.
form.keys.note = A source's diminishing returns name one of these. Each value it reads keeps its own count, so one spot or one creature over and over pays less.
form.keys.cell = Area size
form.keys.cell.hint = Count each area of the world apart, in cubes this many blocks wide. 1 is each block. 0 leaves the place out.
form.keys.target = By kind
form.keys.target.hint = Count each kind of block, creature or item apart.
form.keys.qualifier = By weapon
form.keys.qualifier.hint = Count each weapon or other detail of the moment apart.
form.keys.victim = By creature
form.keys.victim.hint = Count each single creature or player apart, not just its kind.
form.keys.station = By station
form.keys.station.hint = Count each station a moment was worked at apart.
form.settings.title = Track Settings
form.settings.desc = How every track pays on this server, beside what each track says.
form.settings.heading.idle = Idle players
form.settings.idle = Minutes before idle
form.settings.idle.hint = After this many minutes without moving, looking around or using anything, a player earns nothing until they move again. 0 never stops them.
form.sources.title = XP Sources
form.sources.desc = What each moment pays onto a track: blocks broken, creatures killed, hits, placements. Pick one to change it.
form.sources.on = On
form.sources.on.hint = Off pays nothing from this source, so a broader one can pay those moments instead.
form.sources.heading.pays = What it pays
form.sources.pays.note = The most specific row the player's level has reached pays. Below a row's level, the next matching row pays instead.
form.sources.rows = Rows
form.sources.rows.hint = Each row is a name pattern, an equals sign and what it pays, with an at sign and a level if it waits for one, split by commas: Ore_Iron*=50@10, Ore_*=6. A row you leave out keeps what it usually pays. A row of 0 pays nothing, and no broader row pays in its place.
form.sources.xp = For anything else
form.sources.xp.hint = What a moment no row covers pays.
form.sources.peramount = Per point
form.sources.peramount.hint = What each point of the moment pays when no row covers it: a point of damage, a block walked.
form.sources.permaxhealth = Per point of health
form.sources.permaxhealth.hint = What each point of the creature's full health pays when no row covers it.
form.sources.max = Most per moment
form.sources.max.hint = The most one moment pays from any row without a cap of its own. 0 sets no limit.
form.sources.heading.guards = Against farming
form.sources.spawners = Skip spawner mobs
form.sources.spawners.hint = Pay nothing for a creature a spawner, a spawn beacon or a spawn egg stood up.
form.sources.stand = Seconds to stand
form.sources.stand.hint = Pay a placed block only once it has stood this long, still the same block and still the player's. 0 pays at once.
form.sources.heading.diminish = Diminishing returns
form.sources.diminish.note = Each moment counts once in the window and pays at that step. Leave the steps empty to pay every moment in full.
form.sources.steps = Steps
form.sources.steps.hint = What each moment in the window pays, in order, split by commas: 1, 1, 0.5, 0. Every moment past the end pays the last again.
form.sources.window = Window
form.sources.window.hint = When the count starts over: Daily, Weekly, or a rolling span such as 10m, 2h or 1d.
form.sources.key = Count per
form.sources.key.hint = A diminishing key: Cell16, Position, Target, Station, Victim, or one of your own. Empty counts every moment of the source together.
# The World Rules screen's switch for every rule at once, above its list (the file's own $Enabled).
form.rules.heading.all = Every rule
form.rules.all = World rules apply
form.rules.all.hint = Off switches every world rule off at once, in every world: tracks gain and picks grant there as anywhere else. Each rule keeps its own settings for when you switch this back on.
